1: # Physical gamma and the orientation of the source page
2: 
3: Independent orientation audit, 17 November 2026.
4: 
5: Use physical source complex coordinates, and write the line
6: character as \(V=r e^{i\phi}\). The complex threefold orientation is
7: \[
8:  \operatorname{or}(X)=\operatorname{or}(S)\,dr\,d\phi .
9: \]
10: The physical delta circle is positive \(d\phi\). Moving its vector
11: past the four source vectors and the one radial vector gives
12: \[
13:  \operatorname{or}(Y)
14:                   =-\operatorname{or}(S)\,d\log r .   \tag{GO.1}
15: \]
16: Equivalently, if \(V=e^{2\pi i\zeta_2}\) and
17: \(\zeta_2=x+iy\), delta is the positive \(x\)-direction and the
18: orbit orientation is \(\operatorname{or}(S)\,dy\).
19: 
20: For the actual contracting suspension
21: \[
22:  B(a,V)=(a-g,\ e^{2\pi iC}q r_0^m V),
23: \]
24: where \(r_0\) now denotes the family parameter, the inward period
25: is
26: \[
27:  \gamma_{\rm in}=(-g,C+s+mv),\qquad
28:  s=\frac{\log q}{2\pi i},\quad
29:  v=\frac{\log r_0}{2\pi i}.
30: \]
31: Its positive direction decreases the physical line radius.
32: Thus (GO.1) is source-page-first followed by
33: \(\gamma_{\rm in}\). For the inverse period
34: \(\gamma_{\rm out}=-\gamma_{\rm in}\), it is the negative of
35: source-page-first followed by \(\gamma_{\rm out}\).
36: This is an orientation calculation in the physical coordinates;
37: it is not a relabeling of a chosen generator.
38: 
39: For OS45 the cap map is explicitly cap-to-ordinary:
40: \[
41:  \Psi_v(\zeta,t)=\zeta+
42:              \frac{\log t}{2\pi i}\gamma_{\rm in}(v).
43: \]
44: A positive cap meridian becomes the ordinary base meridian plus
45: \(\gamma_{\rm in}\). The ordinary and cap parameter decks are
46: \[
47:  D_{\rm ord}=-\frac{\log((t-t_c)/t)}{2\pi i}\delta,\qquad
48:  D_{\rm cap}=-\frac{\log(t-t_c)}{2\pi i}\delta.
49: \]
50: Since \(\gamma_{\rm in}(v+1)-\gamma_{\rm in}(v)=\delta\),
51: they satisfy the literal square
52: \[
53:  D_{\rm ord}\Psi_v=\Psi_{v+1}D_{\rm cap}.
54: \]
55: Near the cusp this is the deck \(-s\delta\) in P3K.10.
56: Its two extending origins have differences
57: \(\Delta o=-s\delta\) and
58: \(\Delta\sigma=-s\delta+\gamma_{\rm in}\).
59: Because the local coordinates are \(\zeta-o\) and
60: \(\zeta-\sigma\), their cusp-to-ordinary transition is
61: \(\sigma-o\), with positive angular increment
62: \(\gamma_{\rm in}\). The actual positive scalar loop therefore
63: has the positive source-page orientation required in P3K.7.
64: The OS45 index \(-3\) and the primitive-source signs of P3K.22
65: are unchanged.
66: 
67: For the corrected reduced-III construction, the declared
68: ordinary-to-cap map instead gives cusp deck \(+s\delta\), and
69: the corrected origin difference is a positive turn of
70: \(\gamma_{\rm out}=B^{-1}\). Its weighted-S3 map sends that
71: outward period to the positive Hopf circle. Equation (GO.1)
72: then says that the product of its complex source page with that
73: Hopf orientation is opposite the actual orbit orientation.
74: This observation alone does not determine the return sign.
75: The following normal-sphere calculation retains the actual
76: boundary and meridian orientations and completes the comparison.
77: 
78: ## The signed boundary-degree version of P3K.7
79: 
80: Orient the graph page by its complex source orientation. Define
81: \(\kappa\in\{1,-1\}\) by the actual boundary parametrization
82: \[
83:                   \partial V=\kappa\,E\times S^1_\theta ,
84: \]
85: where \(\theta\) is the positive physical parameter direction
86: of the angular trace. Orient the compression by
87: \(\partial W=F-E\). Its product with the parameter circle
88: must then be attached with orientation \(\kappa\); hence
89: \[
90:                          \partial X=\kappa F\times S^1_\theta .
91: \]
92: 
93: The fixed-circle quotient orientation is the one already
94: calculated in P3K.7:
95: \[
96:  \operatorname{or}(Y)=
97:        \operatorname{or}(F)\operatorname{or}(\nu_{\rm Hopf}).
98: \]
99: On the outer radial collar of \(Z=Y\times D^2\), this is
100: \[
101:  \operatorname{or}(Z)=
102:        \operatorname{or}(F)\operatorname{or}(\nu_{\rm Hopf})
103:                    \,dr\,d\theta .
104: \]
105: The trace has orientation
106: \(\kappa\,\operatorname{or}(F)\,dr\,d\theta\).
107: Moving the three normal vectors past the two radial/parameter
108: vectors introduces no sign. Consequently the induced oriented
109: normal three-plane is \(\kappa\nu_{\rm Hopf}\).
110: The actual Euler line \(x\) therefore has
111: \[
112:                          \pi_*x=\kappa
113: \]
114: on the oriented normal sphere bundle, not an automatically
115: positive fibre integral.
116: 
117: Put \(\widehat x=\kappa x\), so \(\pi_*\widehat x=1\), and define
118: \(b\) by \(e_v=2\widehat x-\pi^*b\).
119: The graph section has zero vertical Euler class, so
120: \(b|_V=2\kappa c_1(M)\). Its square is \(4M_{\rm rel}^2\),
121: independent of \(\kappa\). The two bordism-boundary reversals
122: and Jin's inverse mapping-torus convention remain exactly as
123: in P3K.7. Fibre integration therefore gives
124: \[
125:  \begin{aligned}
126:  A_{\rm Jin}
127:   &=\frac{4\int_Bx^3-\int_Bp_1(TB)x}{24}\\
128:   &=\kappa\,
129:       \frac{3\int_{\bar X}b^2-\int_{\bar X}p_1(T\bar X)}{24}.
130:                                                         \tag{GO.2}
131:  \end{aligned}
132: \]
133: This calculation identifies the sign with the actual boundary
134: degree \(\kappa\); an ambient/product-orientation comparison
135: without the normal meridian does not supply it.
136: 
137: For the corrected reduced-III weighted page,
138: \(t=t_*+a^{-m}\). Its compact affine page has complex boundary
139: given by positive \(\arg a\) at large \(|a|\).
140: In the explicit embedding
141: \((a,b)\mapsto(\rho a,\rho^m b)\), \(b-t_*a^m=1\),
142: the positive Hopf parameter \(\gamma_{\rm out}\) is precisely
143: that positive \(\arg a\) direction at the binding.
144: The corrected origin computation makes the positive
145: parameter turn \(+\gamma_{\rm out}\). Thus \(\kappa=+1\).
146: Equation (GO.2) retains the negative value
147: \[
148:                     A=-(3m-1)/4
149: \]
150: for that construction. The OS45 cap-to-ordinary construction
151: likewise has \(\kappa=+1\), with its inward gamma.
152: The earlier suggestion that the ambient reversal by itself
153: would invert the reduced-III index was incomplete; the
154: explicit meridian calculation above supplies the full sign.
